{"availability":"available","full":"mohamed-adhd/streak-saver","name":"streak-saver","description":"Serverless FastAPI backend (Vercel Cron + Upstash Redis) that verifies daily GitHub commits via PyGithub and auto-commits when missed, paired with a C#/Avalonia MVVM setup client.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-26T21:18:42Z","updated":"2026-10-03T22:47:05Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://streak-saver-six.vercel.app","topics":["cron","deployment","python","upstash-redis","vercel"],"demo":"https://streak-saver-six.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:30.244Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:30.244Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:30.244Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T15:46:30.244Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A Vercel-hosted watchdog that keeps your GitHub contribution streak alive — checks if you've committed today, and if not, either commits for you or spams you with increasingly unhinged emails until you do. Paired with a small Avalonia desktop app for one-time setup.","Your GitHub token is encrypted with Fernet before it's stored in Upstash Redis, so the backend never keeps it in plaintext. Alongside the auto-commit safety net, there's an email-alert system that fires off increasingly chaotic \"get back to work\" emails in the hours before the streak would break, in case you'd rather save it yourself.","github streak is not something i can break , like literally i get sick if i dont commit and push at least 7 times a day, but better be safe than sorry , so this is here just in case the electricity cuts or something unexpected happens , 9/10 times i wont even need it"],"features":["DISCLAIMER : this project doesn't inflate commits , the app is allowed to only commit 1 time if i miss my day just to preserve my streak , it cannot inflate or fake commits","streak-saver is a two-part p